An ingest whose next file cannot be created, with no memory to publish the
degraded state, throws std::bad_alloc in the I/O error's place. Both the
mid-slice rotation and the one after the last chunk. Reverts #618.
Guarded-by: "alloc sweep: ingest whose rotation cannot create a file"

